From bd81165ed90f9c953bd349f16187418044e34c50 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ferdinand Vanmaele <info@fvanmaele.de>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 04:10:54 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] [clangd] Index navigation: all symbols at the cursor's
 range are targets

A shard can record several symbols at the same range: on a real project a
call to std::visit was recorded as referring to two declarations. Keeping only
one of them lost references of the other (14 references instead of the AST
path's 15 distinct). symbolsAtFromShard now returns all symbols at the
innermost range; definitions are answered once all of them are known (symbols
located at the same place are reported once), and references are the union,
deduplicated by location with combined attributes. On that project the index
answer now contains every distinct location of the AST answer, plus the call
under the cursor, which the AST answer lacked; the AST answer also listed
locations twice.

ClangdTests 1410/1410 (new: AllSymbolsAtTheSameRangeAreTargets).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
